basis_evidence:
the buyer's country: the value differs by the country chosen for the address. S02-WC-103: 'Fields that change dynamically based on the chosen country of a user (address 1, address 2, city, state, postcode) cannot have custom validation rules, e.g., required fields are determined by locale, not by your settings.'; S02-WC-150: 'These locales override the default country selections after a country is chosen.' (WooCommerce's term 'country locale settings', terms.tsv); the locale of each country code, S02-WC-151: `'AE' => array( 'postcode' => array( 'required' => false, 'hidden' => true, ), 'state' => array( 'required' => false, ), ),` and `'US' => array( 'postcode' => array( 'label' => __( 'ZIP Code', 'woocommerce' ), ), 'state' => array( 'label' => __( 'State', 'woocommerce' ), ), ),`; S02-WC-156: `Country cannot be hidden or optional via locale — it is the lookup key for locale resolution.`; S02-WC-158: `$locale = $this->get_country_locale(); if ( isset( $locale[ $country ] ) ) {`; S02-WC-159: 'The locales/default locales apply on top based * on country selection.'; the fields a locale changes are the billing and shipping address's: S02-WC-149: `'address_1' => '#billing_address_1_field, #shipping_address_1_field',`; the locales kept are those of the countries the store sells or ships to: S02-WC-152: `$locale = array_intersect_key( $locale, array_merge( $this->get_allowed_countries(), $this->get_shipping_countries() ) );` (a reading of the code); the default fields a country's locale overrides: S02-WC-146: 'Returns the fields we show by default.', S02-WC-147: `'country' => array( 'type' => 'country', 'label' => __( 'Country / Region', 'woocommerce' ), 'required' => true,`, S02-WC-148: `$default_address_fields = apply_filters( 'woocommerce_default_address_fields', $fields );`, S02-WC-153: `$locale['default'] = apply_filters( 'woocommerce_get_country_locale_default', $this->get_default_address_fields() );`; the states of each country, a run of one list in i18n/states.php (rule 5, Lists): S02-WC-160: 'Returns an array of country states.' and S02-WC-163: 'Countries defined with empty arrays have no states. These should also be defined in class-wc-countries.php to mark the state field as not required and hidden.'; the format an address is shown in follows its country: S02-WC-142: 'These define how addresses are formatted for display in various countries.' (WooCommerce's term 'address formats', terms.tsv), S02-WC-143: `'US' => "{name}
{company}
{address_1}
{address_2}
{city}, {state_code} {postcode}
{country}",` and S02-WC-144: `// Get format for the address' country.`. Readings: the address a country is chosen for is the buyer's billing or shipping address, which S02-WC-149 names; the formats of S02-WC-142 to S02-WC-144 are those of any address, the buyer's among them; second pass: a postcode is validated by the rule of its address's country, the buyer's among them (a reading, as for the address formats). S02-WC-304: 'Validate a postcode if a shared rule exists for its country.'; S02-WC-306, the checkout's billing and shipping postcode: `$country = $this->get_fieldset_country( $fieldset_key, $data );`; S02-WC-305, S02-WC-307 (Store API), S02-WC-308 (My account) and S02-WC-309 (the cart's shipping calculator): `WC_Validation::is_postcode` with the address's country

the platform: 'we', 'by default', or the release's own code and files (rule 4). S02-WC-103: 'required fields are determined by locale, not by your settings' (the locale being the platform's own, S02-WC-150 and S02-WC-151: a reading); S02-WC-146: 'Returns the fields we show by default.'; the values the release's code sets: the default fields, S02-WC-147: `'postcode' => array( 'label' => __( 'Postcode / ZIP', 'woocommerce' ), 'required' => true,`; each country's locale, S02-WC-151: `'AE' => array( 'postcode' => array( 'required' => false, 'hidden' => true, ), 'state' => array( 'required' => false, ), ),`; the formats, S02-WC-143: `'default' => "{name}
{company}
{address_1}
{address_2}
{city}
{state}
{postcode}
{country}",`, and the base country's address shown without its country unless a filter forces it, S02-WC-145: `! apply_filters( 'woocommerce_formatted_address_force_country_display', false )`; the states, from the release's own file, S02-WC-157: `apply_filters( 'woocommerce_states', include WC()->plugin_path() . '/i18n/states.php' )`. Readings of the code: the values are the release's own; the filters they pass through name no party; second pass: the release's own code and rules, and 'our policy' (rule 4). S02-WC-303: 'Provides postcode validation from the shared PHP/JavaScript rule artifact.'; S02-WC-304: 'Validate a postcode if a shared rule exists for its country.', with S02-WC-305 to S02-WC-309, the code that validates by it; S02-WC-327, on the lists of countries and subdivisions: 'our policy is only to accept changes if they align with the current version of the CLDR project'
